MR_604
Reviewers: Ben Liu, Peter Robinson (He/Him)

* Adds support for review rules to GRAPE

* Review rules are used to create approval rules in GitLab

* Reviewers are encoded in the merge request description

* Reviewers/approval rules are flattened to just the reviewers in Atlassian

* If no review rules are specified, falls back to a default rule provided by GRAPE. Otherwise, the GRAPE rule is not used.

* Reviewers and approval rules can now be removed with --reviewers=\"\" or --reviewers=\"{rule}:\"

* Old rules can be marked as inactive (they must be kept around so that the corresponding GitLab approval rules can be deleted for existing merge requests)

* Old rules can be mapped to new rules

* If no review rules or only one review rule, --reviewers=\"username1,username2\" defaults to the GRAPE fallback rule or the single provided rule

* If more than one review rule, a default rule can be specified in the .grapeconfig file

* Rules can be specified when adding reviewers: --reviewers=\"{rule1}:username1,username2 {rule2}:username3\"

* If a default rule is specified, the rule name can be left off: --reviewers=\"username1,username2 {rule2}:username3\"

* In order to get people ready for the review rule syntax, there is now a warning for when reviewers are separated by a space instead of a comma. That's to prevent issues like the following: --reviewers=\"{rule1}:username1 username2\", which assigned username1 to rule1 and username2 to the default rule.

Here's an example of what can be added to the .grapeconfig file:

'''

[review]

rules = code dc

defaultrule = code

[review-code]

label = GRAPE: Code Review // defaults to GRAPE: {rulename}

minnumreviewers = 2 // defaults to 1

// eligiblereviewers defaults to all

// repositories defaults to all

[review-dc]

label = GRAPE: DC Review

minnumreviewers = 1

eligiblereviewers = benliu dawson24 # A regex can be used

repositories = test_subproject_1 # A regex can be used

'''

